==================================================
PWA — INSTALLABLE APP (SERVICE WORKER + MANIFEST) — REQUIRED
==================================================

This card is a Progressive Web App. It MUST be installable on Android (Chrome), Windows (Chrome/Edge), and iOS (Safari). Two supported flows:
1. ANDROID / WINDOWS / DESKTOP: modern browsers surface the install themselves — capture beforeinstallprompt and trigger it from a visible button (the standard install UI takes over).
2. APPLE IOS: Safari has NO install prompt — the only path is Share → "Add to Home Screen", so the card MUST show the iOS tutorial modal (see "ADD TO HOME SCREEN / INSTALL MODAL").

IMPLEMENTATION (all client-side, inside ONE guarded useEffect; typeof window !== "undefined"):
1. WEB APP MANIFEST (Blob URL):
   - Build: { name: AGENCY (fallback FULL_NAME), short_name: AGENCY (truncated to ~12 chars, fallback FIRST NAME), description: TAGLINE, start_url: cardUrl, scope: "/", display: "standalone", orientation: "portrait", background_color: {{BACKGROUND}}, theme_color: {{PRIMARY}}, icons: [{ src: {{AVATAR_URL}}, sizes: "any", type: "image/*", purpose: "any" }] }. The app icon MUST be the AGENT PROFILE PICTURE.
   - URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(manifest)], { type: "application/manifest+json" })) then append <link rel="manifest" href={blobUrl} /> to document.head.
2. SERVICE WORKER (Blob URL registration):
   - const swCode = "self.addEventListener('install',()=>self.skipWaiting());self.addEventListener('activate',(e)=>e.waitUntil(clients.claim()));self.addEventListener('fetch',(e)=>{});";
   - navigator.serviceWorker.register(URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([swCode], { type: "text/javascript" }))).catch(() => {}). Works in Chrome/Edge/Android. Wrap in try/catch so any failure silently degrades — the card still works as a normal page. This also makes the browser suggest/trigger PWA installation by itself on Android/Windows (the normal flow).
3. APPLE TAGS + LOADING/SPLASH (the agent profile pic is BOTH the app icon AND the loading/splash image):
   - <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href={{AVATAR_URL}} /> — iOS home-screen icon. If {{AVATAR_URL}} is empty, use {{COVER_URL}}, then the first gallery image; never a generic placeholder.
   - <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />, <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent" />, <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content={{FULL_NAME}} />.
   - <meta name="theme-color" content={{BACKGROUND}} /> and <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />.
   - Append all of these imperatively to document.head inside the guarded useEffect (allowed — see NO DYNAMIC FEATURES note).
4. INSTALL PROMPT (Android/Windows/desktop):
   - let deferredPrompt = null;
   - window.addEventListener("beforeinstallprompt", (e) => { e.preventDefault(); deferredPrompt = e; });
   - An "Install app" affordance (the A2HS modal, or a small floating pill near the bottom HUD) appears when deferredPrompt is set; on tap: deferredPrompt.prompt(); await deferredPrompt.userChoice; deferredPrompt = null;
   - Listen for "appinstalled" → flip the UI to "installed".
5. PLATFORM GATING:
   - const isIOS = /iPad|iPhone|iPod/.test(navigator.userAgent) && !window.MSStream;
   - const isStandalone = window.matchMedia("(display-mode: standalone)").matches || window.navigator.standalone === true;
   - If isIOS && !isStandalone → show the iOS Share-to-Home-Screen tutorial modal.
   - Else if deferredPrompt → show "Install App".
   - Else if isStandalone → show "App is installed — launch it from your home screen".
   - Else → show the generic hint (address-bar install icon / browser menu).
6. NEVER show any install UI when the app is already running standalone.

